@WE 2211. Tricks of Spirits.

@WE 2823. Spirits do not know what they are going to say until they have said it.

@WE 4575. Evil Spirits are not deliberately deceitful, but weave their poisonous wiles as it were unknowingly; thus their nature acts. @SE 253. @1043.

@WE 6155. How evil Spirits can personate others.

@SE 7. Spirits induce dreams; and, when man sleeps, they dream in like manner. @664. @1882. @2436.

@18. Spirits speak freely with man if he does not reflect upon the nature of it. They cannot bear that Spirits coming from some other place should speak with the man. One knows not of the presence of another. When they are not spoken to, they know no otherwise than that they are the man.

@68. It displeases Spirits that man should answer and explore their genius, and should rule them. @3563.

@78. (Index, under _Memoria_). Spirits and Angels have their sensuous memory from the man with whom they are.

@120. The Spirits with a man are as the man; learned with the learned, stupid with the stupid...

