@--. All Spirits are first in the World of Spirits, and are then with men who live in the world, evil Spirits with the evil, and good Spirits with the good; and through these man has communication and conjunction either with the Hells, or with the Heavens.

@556[17]. Such was the deaf and dumb Spirit whom the Lord cast out. Explained.

@586[2]. Every man is in company with Spirits. Explained.

@587[5]. "No breath in them" (Jeremiah 10:14) = no spiritual life.

@618. Spirits and Angels have taste equally with men, but their taste flows from a spiritual origin...

@624[8]. "I will pour out My spirit" (Joel 2:28) = the Divine truth proceeding from Him.

@629[15]. "He giveth not the spirit by measure" (John 3:34) = the Divine truth, and the derivative intelligence and wisdom.

@654[42]. "Not spirit" (Isaiah 31:3) = no life from the Lord.

@665[end]. "Spirit" = the reception of the influx of Divine truth, and the derivative spiritual life. Illustrated. @666[3].

@684[32]. "The breath of our nostrils" (Lamentations 4:20) = the life of the perception of good and truth.

@727[22]. "The spirit of scortations" (Hosea 4:12) = the cupidity of falsifying.

@730[23]. "The spirit poured upon us from on high" (Isaiah 32:15) = influx from Heaven into them.

@731[end]. "The unclean Spirit going out of the man" = the removal of evils and falsities from the man who performs repentance.

