Spy. See <Explore>, <Watchman>.

Squalor.; Squallor.
Squalid.; Squallidus.

@AC 4054[end]. They live in squalor.

@5246[2]. A state of temptation is relatively squalid and unclean.

@HH 182. They appear in garments torn, squalid, and disgusting.

@488[6]. They who have taken delight in adulteries live where all things are sordid and squalid: these they love.

