Square.; Quadratus.
Square, To.; Quadrare.
See <Foursquare>.

@AC 5952[end]. This squares with it.

@9717. "The altar shall be foursquare" (Exodus 27:1) = what is just.

@--. In the other life, the goods of the external man, which are called just, are presented as square. Hence it is that by "what is square" is signified what is just. Illustrated.

@9861. "Foursquare it shall be doubled" (Exodus 28:16) = what is just and perfect.

@10180. "Foursquare shall it be" (Exodus 30:2) = what is perfect; for "foursquare" = what is just, and also what is perfect.

@10770. Small square pieces of bread seen.

@HH 355[end]. These square with the light of the Spiritual World.

@464[2]. The things which do not square with them cannot be uttered.

@NJHD 1[5]. What is quadrangular or foursquare = what is perfect. References.

@DP 335[3]. As is said concerning squaring the circle.

@AR 905. See <Foursquare>.

@CL 103[3]. I saw that the house was square, the sides looking to the quarters.

@132. Around the theatre, in a square form, were placed seats.

@263. The devil had on a square cap.

@TCR 22. For this squares with its essence.

@134. A square temple seen.

@353[end]. Compared to a battalion formed in a square.

@367[6]. This comparison squares.

@469. This squares with the Divine justice.

@508. Another temple in a square form seen.

@SE 2626. Bread cut into square bits: its correspondence.

@4627[4]. The particulars then do not square with the general.

@AE 205[4]. These things are not applicable to David.

Squinting. See <Strabismus>.

